.IX Title "FPING6 8"
.TH FPING6 8 "2022-02-07" "BACKWARDS-COMPATIBILITY" ""
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
fping6 \- backwards compatibility with fping below version 4.0
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBfping6\fR [ \fIoptions\fR ] [ \fIsystems...\fR ]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBfping6\fR is a backwards-compatibility symbolic link to \fBfping\fR
solely for the purpose to be able to specify Smokeping remote
configurations which work on systems with fping ≥ 4.0 as well as on
systems with fping < 4.0.
.PP
Please do \fInot\fR use fping in in scripts or configurations which don't
require it for backwards-compatibility with older fping versions. It
will vanish as soon as it's no more required in setups as mentioned
above.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\f(CWfping(8)\fR
.SH "AUTHOR"
.IX Header "AUTHOR"
